{%- comment -%} cx-buybox-core — the ENTIRE buy-box widget, rendered verbatim by both thin block wrappers. MINIFIED ON PURPOSE (total-Liquid deploy budget): full exposition of THE LIQUID RULES (RULE 1 never capture, assign or echo a render; RULE 2 t returns already-escaped HTML, RAW/SAFE string spaces), params, group ownership and history live in README "Core snippet internals". Editor note: comments here carry NO Liquid delimiters and no pipe characters (harness fidelity lint). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product != blank and product.selling_plan_groups.size > 0 -%}
{%- liquid
# OWNERSHIP: render OUR allow-listed group or render NOTHING; no allow-list means no widget. TWO factors, BOTH mandatory: (a) the group's app_id equals cx_allow.appId; (b) one of the group's OWN selling plan ids is in cx_allow.planIds, exact string equality, never a joined list. App ids and plan ids read the same way from the Admin API and Storefront Liquid, unlike a SellingPlanGroup's own id (a different, opaque per-shop id in each), so app_id replaces the old group-id compare as the real second factor. A metafield published before appId existed fails closed until the next sync republishes it. Full essay: README "Core snippet internals"; proof: tests/liquid/two-apps.test.ts.
assign cx_allow = shop.metafields.cellexia.plan_groups.value
assign cx_allow_plan_ids = cx_allow.planIds
assign cx_allow_plan_count = cx_allow_plan_ids | size
assign cx_allow_app_id = cx_allow.appId | append: ''
assign cx_group = false
assign cx_group_found = false
if cx_allow_plan_count > 0 and cx_allow_app_id != blank
for cx_g in product.selling_plan_groups
assign cx_own = false
assign cx_g_app_id = cx_g.app_id | append: ''
if cx_g_app_id == cx_allow_app_id
for cx_p in cx_g.selling_plans
assign cx_p_id = cx_p.id | append: ''
for cx_allowed_plan in cx_allow_plan_ids
assign cx_allowed_plan_id = cx_allowed_plan | append: ''
if cx_allowed_plan_id == cx_p_id
assign cx_own = true
break
endif
endfor
if cx_own
break
endif
endfor
endif
# A group matching neither factor is skipped, not fatal: a later group may be genuinely ours. First match wins, in product order.
if cx_own
assign cx_group = cx_g
assign cx_group_found = true
break
endif
endfor
endif
-%}
{%- if cx_group_found -%}
{%- comment -%} From here to the matching else branch: the widget itself (the render snapshot pins the output). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
